# Chakra Sentinel configuration. Installed to /etc/chakra/sentinel.conf.
#
# Sentinel works fully offline out of the box: a deterministic
# pattern-matching Intent Engine routes your question to one of the
# Chakra system API tools (chakra-health, chakra-processlens, etc.),
# runs it, and shows you the result. No setup, no internet, no API key.
#
# NVIDIA NIM integration is OPTIONAL and OFF by default. If you set
# NIM_API_KEY below, Sentinel additionally sends the ALREADY-COLLECTED
# tool output to NVIDIA's hosted API and asks it to explain the result
# in plainer language. The AI never decides which tool to run or gets
# raw system access -- it only ever sees data the deterministic,
# Risk-0-only dispatcher already fetched. This matches the master
# manual's own AI safety principle: AI -> Structured Intent -> Policy
# Validator -> Approved Chakra API, never AI -> raw shell.
#
# Get a free API key at https://build.nvidia.com (NVIDIA account
# required). Queries sent to NIM leave this machine -- if that's not
# acceptable for your use, just leave NIM_API_KEY blank.

NIM_API_KEY=
NIM_MODEL=meta/llama-3.1-8b-instruct
NIM_BASE_URL=https://integrate.api.nvidia.com/v1
